---
import Funnel from '../layouts/Funnel.astro';
import BrandHeader from '../components/BrandHeader.astro';
import BrandFooter from '../components/BrandFooter.astro';
import FirstPractice from '../components/FirstPractice.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import {funnelConfig,safeWebUrl} from '../lib/funnel-config';
import '../styles/funnel-v5.css';
const videoUrl=safeWebUrl(funnelConfig.videoUrl);
const captionsUrl=safeWebUrl(funnelConfig.captionsUrl);
const checkoutUrl=safeWebUrl(funnelConfig.checkoutUrl);
const canPurchase=funnelConfig.salesOpen&&checkoutUrl;
---
<Funnel title="Start changing the pattern | Protocol 44" description="Put the first Protocol 44 lesson into practice: map a setback, notice your response and choose one action to try differently.">
  <BrandHeader page="vsl" />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="v5-vsl-opening wrap" aria-labelledby="vsl-title"><h1 id="vsl-title">Start changing<br /><span>the pattern.</span></h1><p id="vsl-context" class="lead">Take one recent setback and work out where you could respond differently. This free exercise from the first Protocol 44 lesson turns reflection into a specific next step.</p><a href="#first-practice" class="hero-secondary">Go to the exercise <Arrow /></a><div class="v5-film">{videoUrl&&<div class="video-frame" id="film"><video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/brand/vsl-poster.png" aria-label="Protocol 44 introduction"><source src={videoUrl}/>{captionsUrl&&<track kind="captions" src={captionsUrl} srclang="en" label="English" default/>}Your browser cannot play the video. <a href={videoUrl}>Open the video</a>.</video></div>}{!videoUrl&&<p class="film-update">We’re preparing the video introduction. The written exercise is ready below.</p>}{videoUrl&&<p id="video-error" class="video-error" role="status" hidden>The video could not be loaded. Try again or use the written practice below.</p>}{videoUrl&&funnelConfig.transcript&&<details class="transcript"><summary>Read the film transcript</summary><p>{funnelConfig.transcript}</p></details>}</div></section>
    <section class="vsl-lesson-intro wrap" data-motion><h2>Catch the thought.<br />Choose your response.</h2><div><p class="lead">A missed plan can turn into “I never follow through.” A request can get an automatic yes. A money worry can become another week of avoiding a decision.</p><p>Choose a recent example. Write down what happened, what you told yourself and what you did next. Include the practical constraints, such as time, money or other responsibilities.</p><p>Then choose a response you can practice: review one bill, ask for time before saying yes, or return to a plan you put aside. Say when you’ll try it.</p><p id="preferred-format" class="availability-note" hidden></p></div></section>
    <FirstPractice />
    <section class="vsl-next"><div class="wrap"><h2>Build on this<br />first step.</h2><div><p>This exercise begins with one situation. The planned 22 lessons and 22 audio practices go on to explore learned expectations, choices, boundaries and following through. Each phase gives you something to put into practice.</p>{canPurchase?<a class="button button-dark" href={checkoutUrl}>Join Protocol 44 <Arrow /></a>:<a class="button button-dark" href="/#inside">See how the program works <Arrow /></a>}<p class="button-note">{canPurchase?'Review access and purchase terms at checkout.':'The full program and recordings are still in preparation.'}</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="faq-section wrap" aria-labelledby="practice-faq-title"><h2 id="practice-faq-title">If you get stuck</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>What if I don’t know why I do this?</summary><p>You can leave that question open. Write about something you remember and what you noticed at the time. You don’t need an explanation for everything.</p></details><details><summary>What if I can’t do what I planned?</summary><p>Choose a smaller step or a different time. If you planned to review your spending, opening a bill might be enough to get started. Adjust the plan to what’s possible.</p></details><details><summary>How do I know when I’m done?</summary><p>You’re done when you’ve described the situation and chosen something to try next. You can come back to your notes afterward and see what you’d change.</p></details><details><summary>Where is my writing saved?</summary><p>The form does not send your writing anywhere or keep it after the page is reloaded. Use “Download my reflection” to save a text file on your device.</p></details></div></section>
  </main><BrandFooter />
  <script>
    import '../lib/page-motion';
    const video=document.querySelector('video');const error=document.getElementById('video-error');
    const failed=()=>{if(error)error.hidden=false;};video?.addEventListener('error',failed);video?.querySelector('source')?.addEventListener('error',failed);video?.addEventListener('loadeddata',()=>{if(error)error.hidden=true;});
  </script>
</Funnel>
